import shark1 from '../assets/MyKin/MyKinTshirts/shark1.jpg';
import shark2 from '../assets/MyKin/MyKinTshirts/shark2.jpg';
const pageTitle = "Mykin Shop";
---
<Layout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <h2>2025 MyKin Pop-up Shop</h2>
  <p>Mykin was a creative pop-up shop currated entirely by students with 
    the support of Michael Salter in the University of Oregon's communication 
    design course in Fall 2025. The shop featured student-designed t-shirts centralized 
    under a collective theme of universal connectivity and community. Mykin was designed as a universe 
    of characters, where each student contributed their own planet of unique characters and designs. 
    Students were encouraged to explore their own styles and narratives while adhering to the overarching theme and 
    contributing to the collective identity of Mykin.
  </p>
  <p>
    My contribution to Mykin was a planet called "Aqualis," centered around aquatic-themed characters. The process included designing and refining
    characters, cutting the design in vinyl, and transferring the design onto shirts using a heat press. I also contributed my ideas to the logo design, 
    tag design, social media posts, and other print media for the shop. Overall, Mykin was a successful project that showcased the class's creativity and 
    sold a total of 74 shirts within the two-hour pop-up shop event.


